A||N||5||DaRkLoRD||Writing a book?||||5||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||11-28-2000||01:14 AM||||Has anyone here either written a non-fiction book, or personally knows someone who has?<P>For a while now I've wanted to write a book.. (try to keep the jokes about my name to a minimum, eh? hehe) but honestly, my writing skills aren't all that great. I'd like to learn about the writing and publishing process, so that I might find a co-author, to put my ideas on paper in a coherent form.<P>any comments are welcome, if I actually manage to do this.. I'll mention all my friends in the dedication.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||11-28-2000||05:39 AM||||My brother has published two books - no bestsellers or anything, but still pretty good books. I'm not very familiar with the business, all I know is that it took a long time after finishing the writing before the books were actually published. But I guess it's more difficult here in Holland to get a book published than in the States because of the relatively small market here (only 15M inhabitants).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-28-2000||08:04 PM||||I've been in the middle of writing a fiction novel for about 6 years.  Some decade I might just finish it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||11-28-2000||10:17 PM||||I had also started on my book about 10 years ago. It is more of a "Jack Handy- Deep Thoughts" kind of book. The title is "One Hundred and One Things My Old Grand Daddy Used to Say". It included some classics like- Come here boy, pull my finger. My wife is an outstanding artist and I believe the illustrations make the book. But we have not worked on it in a few years.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||11-28-2000||10:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>...Come here boy, pull my finger... I believe the illustrations make the book...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>um, what kind of illustration does she have for that one?<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||11-28-2000||10:30 PM||||my book is more along the lines of philosophical musings, on topics relating from politics to school life..<P>I've been thinking about doing this for over a year now, but I became more interested in the last few weeks due to the election fiasco in the USA. One of the things that bugs me, is when people assume that just because they CAN vote, that means they SHOULD vote...<P>2 years ago, I answered the door when a person was handing out election papers for their party. I mentioned I wasn't going to vote, and the lady looked at me with a shocked expression and exclaimed "but it's your right to vote!" so I said "it's also my right NOT to vote." I made that choice because I didn't understand the issues well enough to form a good decision. I don't allow myself to be swayed by the mudslinging that the politicians do during their campaigns, I try to focus on their take on the important issues.<P>I know a few people won't like my opinions, and that's to be expected.. but if you want to say anything bad, please email me privately.. I enjoy discussing this stuff, as it helps me identify flaws in my reasoning, or makes me consider things from a new angle.. and it would also give me counter-arguments to discuss in the book.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
